      "writtenOn": "2026-02-12T13:56:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The thing is, it\u0027s a lie `uint32(2)` is not a c-style cast, it\u0027s a c++ functional style cast. Reading the style guide (https://google.github.io/styleguide/cppguide.html#Casting) I think what I really wanted was `uint32_t{2}` when I did `uint32_t(2)` .\n\n\u003e Use brace initialization to convert arithmetic types (e.g., int64_t{x}). \n\nI\u0027ll try that and see if this still needs to be suppressed.",
      "parentUuid": "be048629_879da1ce",
      "revId": "507fd2b6f7df025b88258e9186c805d03c3d49ea",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
